WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.275
Hold W at a brick pillar in a video world model.

00:00:03.655 --> 00:00:05.588
The raw model walks straight through.

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:08.487
The same input with NoPeWorld stops at the bricks.

00:00:11.502 --> 00:00:12.572
Hi, I'm Kerb.

00:00:12.572 --> 00:00:16.140
These models have no physics engine, so nothing says no.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.351
NoPeWorld adds the no, and leaves the generator alone.

00:00:20.908 --> 00:00:21.467
From above.

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.821
The camera walks at an angled wall, and the raw model's path

00:00:24.821 --> 00:00:25.939
runs right through it.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:29.050
So at every chunk, score 34 candidate motions.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.732
Sweep a disc along each.

00:00:30.732 --> 00:00:33.760
Red would touch the wall, green keeps its margin.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.317
A game engine would slide along the wall.

00:00:36.317 --> 00:00:38.186
Pick the green one closest to that.

00:00:38.606 --> 00:00:41.009
And the camera slides, instead of passing through.

00:00:44.475 --> 00:00:47.768
There is no map at test time, and the generator stays frozen.

00:00:48.168 --> 00:00:51.318
But its hidden states carry the geometry, so the head reads a

00:00:51.318 --> 00:00:52.631
few middle and deep blocks.

00:00:53.031 --> 00:00:57.574
Each candidate is added to every token, and two cross-attention blocks read the grid.

00:00:57.974 --> 00:01:01.060
Out comes a safety and an intent score per candidate.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.602
An unsafe input gets swapped.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:04.738
Why the DiT?

00:01:04.738 --> 00:01:08.490
On decoded pixels the same head is close to a coin flip.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.616
On DiT states it separates safe from unsafe almost perfectly.

00:01:13.308 --> 00:01:16.774
NoPeBench places each generated video on the true map.

00:01:16.774 --> 00:01:22.166
The raw model goes through, or erases, the obstacle on 89 routes of 100.

00:01:22.586 --> 00:01:25.185
With the head in collision mode, 7 are left.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:28.073
Most of the rest are stops, and only 13 slides.

00:01:29.858 --> 00:01:33.875
A depth guard that halts on every chunk has fewer violations on

00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:35.214
average, about ten percent.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:40.852
NoPeWorld lands at sixteen, but it slides instead of freezing, and costs almost nothing.

00:01:42.475 --> 00:01:44.616
The model already knows where its walls are.

00:01:44.616 --> 00:01:47.293
A tiny head turns that into the motion you get.

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:54.875
Thirty-four candidates, read from the DiT, and a camera that stops at the wall.

00:01:54.875 --> 00:01:55.790
Thanks for watching!

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:58.268
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:58.268 --> 00:01:58.856
I'm Kerb.

00:01:58.856 --> 00:01:59.150
Bye!
